    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §314, Exec L (as proposed in S.596 & A.2296)",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8826\n\nSPONSOR: HINCHEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to providing a rebuttable\npresumption relating to recertification as a minority and women-owned\nbusiness enterprise\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to L.2025, C.669.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by narrowing the timeline\nfor, applicability, and scope of the rebuttable presumption and adding\nlanguage clarifying that the Division of Minority and Women's Business\nDevelopment has the authority to review all applications subject to this\npresumption.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 669 of the Laws of 2025.   \nFISCAL IMPLI-\nCATIONS:\n\nNone  \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2025 amending the executive law relating to\nproviding a rebuttable presumption relating to recertification as a\nminority and women-owned business enterprise, as proposed in legislative\nbills numbers S.596 and A.2296, takes effect.\n",
